# VANGUARD Core (Go daemon) -- local .env example.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory as the `vanguard` binary /
# working directory you launch `vanguard serve` from) and fill in real
# values. `.env` is a DEV CONVENIENCE ONLY -- it is loaded by
# core/cmd/vanguard/dotenv.go before flag parsing, and a real environment
# variable always takes precedence over a value from this file.
#
# In production, prefer systemd's `EnvironmentFile=` directive over a
# checked-out `.env` file.
#
# This file is already covered by .gitignore's top-level `.env` pattern --
# never commit your real `.env` with live secrets.

# --- Telegram real-time alerts (optional) ---------------------------------
# Both must be set for Autopilot ban / Panic Mode alerts to be sent. Either
# left blank/unset disables the notifier entirely (a safe no-op, not an
# error). Intentionally env-var only -- never exposed as a CLI flag, since
# flag values leak into `ps aux` output on a shared host.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- Dashboard session security (optional but recommended for prod) -------
# HMAC secret used to sign dashboard session JWTs. If unset, a random
# ephemeral secret is generated per-process (every session is invalidated
# on restart).
VANGUARD_JWT_SECRET=

# Comma-separated fail-safe admin IPs Autopilot can never ban.
VANGUARD_ADMIN_IPS=
